A 2022 arXiv research paper by George Vahala, Linda Vahala, Abhay K. Ram, Min Soe. \bf{Abstract}
: The effect of the thickness of the dielectric boundary layer that connects a material of refractive index
n_{1}
to another of index
n_{2}
is considered for the propagation of an electromagnetic pulse. For very thin boundary layer the scattering properties of the pulse mimics that found from the Fresnel jump conditions for a plane wave - except that the transmission to incident amplitudes are augmented by a factor of
\sqrt{n_{2}/n_{1}}
.
